Subject: Remove the one-off ablation knobs and their branches

What this does
  Deletes the `REGVM_KNOB` ablation switches nothing reads and their
  alternative branches (REGVM_HOMES, REGVM_NOTRANSFER, REGVM_NOELEMXFER,
  REGVM_NOFOLD, REGVM_NOBCPOOL, REGVM_NOCHAIN, REGVM_NOARITH2,
  REGVM_NOINTERNAL, REGVM_NORMW, REGVM_OWN, REGVM_NOCYCLE, REGVM_NOSTUB,
  REGVM_NOPHIIN, REGVM_NOVERIFY, REGVM_FORCE_DEFER, REGVM_PROMO_NOLOC,
  REGVM_PROMO_NOARG, REGVM_ONLY0, REGVM_ONLYSLOT, REGVM_NOPROMO,
  REGVM_OLDPHIUSE, REGVM_NOCOALESCE, REGVM_NOCOAL), plus `REGVM_SKEW`
  (0197) and `REGVM_REPORT_DEFERRED` (0225). `REGVM_HOMES` collapses to its
  shipped mode 5.

Why we need it
  Each was a one-off ablation recorded in a `.local` note, and nothing reads
  any of them. They folded to their default at run time, so every one is an
  alternative branch kept only on paper. `REGVM_BASELINE_ALL` and the
  `REGVM_DUMP*` tools stay.

What it adds
  No new API. Runtime only.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

